---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Docs — Torana">
  <article class="frame prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Documentation</p>
    <h1 class="display">Operate the boundary you already have.</h1>
    <p>Torana is a local reverse proxy for coding-agent and LLM traffic. This documentation hub separates the stable operator path from lower-level ABI material.</p>
    <h2>For operators</h2>
    <table><tbody>
      <tr><th><a href="/quickstart/">Quickstart</a></th><td>Install, configure one provider, and route a harness.</td></tr>
      <tr><th><a href="/plugins/">Plugin registry</a></th><td>Inspect capabilities and install plugins individually.</td></tr>
      <tr><th><a href="https://github.com/torana-edge/torana-edge/blob/main/docs/CONFIGURATION.md">Configuration ↗</a></th><td>Providers, routes, failover, cache, and observability.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <h2>For plugin authors</h2>
    <table><tbody>
      <tr><th><a href="https://github.com/torana-edge/torana-plugin-sdk">SDK repository ↗</a></th><td>Canonical ABI, Go and Rust helpers, templates, and conformance tests.</td></tr>
      <tr><th><a href="https://github.com/torana-edge/torana-plugins">Official plugins ↗</a></th><td>Complete examples with manifests and release bundles.</td></tr>
      <tr><th><a href="https://github.com/torana-edge/torana-edge/tree/main/sdk/pb">Protocol reference ↗</a></th><td>The protobuf contract used at the WASM boundary.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </article>
</Layout>
